<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Command shares continue suspension.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Command shares continue suspension.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Command Petroleum Holdings Ltd said on Tuesday its shares would continue to be suspended due to continued talks with another party that may lead to a merger.</p>
<p>Command is 32.64 percent owned by Snyder Oil Corp of the United States. Shares in the Sydney-based oil group, operator of the Ravva field off the coast of India, have been suspended since last Wednesday after the company announced it was in merger talks. Command shares last traded at 97 cents.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373 1800</p>
</text>
